WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.455
Most PDF-to-Excel demos stop when a spreadsheet appears.

2
00:00:03.455 --> 00:00:04.264
Truecell continues.

3
00:00:04.264 --> 00:00:10.734
It verifies the numbers, shows where every cell came from, and records what happened during review.

4
00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:14.777
This is document extraction built for evidence, not just output.

5
00:00:15.427 --> 00:00:18.937
A basic extraction workflow ends with rows and columns.

6
00:00:18.937 --> 00:00:24.006
Truecell continues through validation, source tracing, explicit human review, and an audit-ready workbook.

7
00:00:24.006 --> 00:00:30.245
Each layer is visible in the application and reproducible from the supplied source, samples, and reports.

8
00:00:30.895 --> 00:00:35.581
Truecell runs locally on CPU, without an API key or cloud AI upload.

9
00:00:35.581 --> 00:00:42.070
It handles native PDFs and scanned documents, detects tables automatically, and accepts files up to two hundred pages.

10
00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.674
The measured evidence shown in this demo covers fifty pages.

11
00:00:46.324 --> 00:00:51.651
In this dummy bank statement, the table appears in seconds, but extraction is only step one.

12
00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.649
Truecell builds a bounded priority queue.

13
00:00:53.649 --> 00:01:00.974
It flags a wrong total, a sparse summary row, and two running-balance breaks while retaining the original page beside the structured grid.

14
00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:07.514
Selecting the balance finding jumps to row eleven, column Z, and outlines the exact source cell.

15
00:01:07.514 --> 00:01:13.035
The evidence drawer retains the original reading, page, source box, extraction engine, and confidence context.

16
00:01:13.035 --> 00:01:16.717
A reviewer can inspect the document before touching the value.

17
00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:22.441
Truecell discovers repeated numeric relationships instead of relying on fixed financial column names.

18
00:01:22.441 --> 00:01:26.734
Fifteen of seventeen eligible rows agree with the inferred balance equation.

19
00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:30.247
The printed value, one thousand eighty-one, breaks two checks.

20
00:01:30.247 --> 00:01:34.150
Two equation instances support a proposal of one thousand sixty-four.

21
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.451
Before editing, Truecell evaluates the proposal on a disposable copy.

22
00:01:38.451 --> 00:01:44.293
Review findings fall from four to two, and failed equation checks fall from two to zero.

23
00:01:44.293 --> 00:01:46.118
The working data remains unchanged.

24
00:01:46.118 --> 00:01:50.865
Agreement is evidence, not permission, so the agent never silently applies the correction.

25
00:01:51.515 --> 00:01:56.881
After checking the source, the reviewer supplies a reason and explicitly saves the corrected value.

26
00:01:56.881 --> 00:02:03.321
The original reading remains available, and the audit rail records the before value, after value, timestamp, and explanation.

27
00:02:03.321 --> 00:02:06.898
This is a traceable human decision, not an invisible rewrite.

28
00:02:07.548 --> 00:02:14.024
Now the difficult case: five raster-only pages, twelve columns, repeated headers, and records split across page boundaries.

29
00:02:14.024 --> 00:02:20.500
Truecell joins all five pages into one table, removes four repeated headers, and recovers both split rows.

30
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:24.309
The join receipt exposes every merge instead of hiding it.

31
00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:29.813
This disclosed stress fixture contains fifty pages, eight hundred rows, and twelve columns.

32
00:02:29.813 --> 00:02:33.173
Searching for invoice eight hundred returns one exact match.

33
00:02:33.173 --> 00:02:38.027
Selecting it moves straight to page fifty and outlines the original source value.

34
00:02:38.027 --> 00:02:40.641
Search never breaks the row-to-page evidence link.

35
00:02:41.291 --> 00:02:45.086
Truecell perturbs disposable copies and reports both detections and misses.

36
00:02:45.086 --> 00:02:50.019
In this live run, fourteen of twenty-four controlled edits raised a new finding.

37
00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:53.055
The untouched source and review history remain safe.

38
00:02:53.055 --> 00:02:58.748
This measures validation sensitivity, not OCR accuracy, and it keeps limitations visible to the judge.

39
00:02:59.398 --> 00:03:02.048
The Excel output is designed for inspection.

40
00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:09.998
Alongside the data, it includes cell evidence, validation findings, the join receipt, page audit, inferred constraints, correction history, verification, and provenance.

41
00:03:09.998 --> 00:03:16.434
Judges can trace a spreadsheet value back to the page and understand how the result was produced.

42
00:03:17.084 --> 00:03:18.997
The claims are deliberately scoped.

43
00:03:18.997 --> 00:03:23.208
Twenty-two of twenty-two disclosed development cases passed their defined exact checks.

44
00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:28.184
The packaged RapidOCR suite passed five of five scan cases with Tesseract excluded.

45
00:03:28.184 --> 00:03:33.160
The public Unicode audit matched one hundred twenty-six of one hundred twenty-six cells.

46
00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:37.371
These are development results, not a promise about every hidden document.

47
00:03:38.021 --> 00:03:40.532
Many tools can extract a table.

48
00:03:40.532 --> 00:03:47.229
Truecell adds what serious document work requires: validation, source evidence, review discipline, and an audit trail.

49
00:03:47.229 --> 00:03:50.577
This is the difference a judge can inspect.

50
00:03:50.577 --> 00:03:50.996
Truecell.

51
00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:52.670
Every cell, accounted for.

